		<p>We do <strong>not</strong> use your data for advertising, and we do <strong>not</strong> track you across other companies' apps or websites.</p>

		<h2>4. In-app purchases (Apple, Google &amp; RevenueCat)</h2>
		<p>Subscriptions and other in-app purchases are made through the <strong>Apple App Store</strong> or <strong>Google Play</strong>. Your payment details are collected and processed by Apple or Google as independent data controllers under <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple's</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's</a> privacy policies. We never receive your card number.</p>
		<p>We use <strong>RevenueCat, Inc.</strong> (USA) as our processor to validate store purchases and keep your plan in sync across devices. RevenueCat receives the store purchase token or receipt, a RevenueCat app user ID linked to your TrophyLog account, and basic device metadata (such as platform, app version, and IP address). We store your subscription status, plan, and purchase identifiers to manage your access and usage limits.</p>

		<h2>5. Content moderation, reports &amp; blocking</h2>
		<p>Content you share with other users (for example in hunting groups, on your profile, or via public or unlisted links) carries your user ID as its author and may be screened, automatically and by our team, for content that violates our <a href="/terms?lang=en">Terms</a>. When you report content or a user, or block a user, we record who reported or blocked whom, the content concerned, the reason you gave, and a snapshot of the content as evidence, so that we can review the report and act on it. The reported user is not told who reported them. We keep a record of the decisions we make so we can enforce our Terms consistently and respond to appeals. Private hunting-log data that you have not shared is not screened.</p>

		<h2>6. Who we share data with</h2>
		<p>We share personal data only with service providers ("processors") that help us run TrophyLog, under data processing agreements:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Railway</strong> — application hosting and database</li>
			<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> (R2, Workers) — storage of your photos and files, database backups, and request routing/delivery for our services</li>
			<li><strong>Bunny Stream</strong> — upload, processing, hosting and playback of videos you add</li>
			<li><strong>Resend</strong> — transactional email (such as verification and account-deletion codes)</li>
			<li><strong>Google Firebase</strong> (Crashlytics, Cloud Messaging) — crash diagnostics and push notifications</li>
			<li><strong>Mapbox</strong> — map rendering (receives location/map requests)</li>
			<li><strong>RevenueCat, Inc.</strong> — in-app purchase validation and subscription management</li>
			<li><strong>Google / Apple</strong> — only if you use Sign in with Google/Apple, for authentication</li>
		</ul>
		<p><strong>Apple and Google</strong> process your in-app purchases as independent controllers, not as our processors. We may disclose personal data to authorities where the law requires it, for example in connection with unlawful content or conduct reported to us. We do not sell your personal data.</p>

		<h2>7. International transfers</h2>
		<p>Some of our processors (e.g. Google, RevenueCat, Cloudflare, Bunny Stream, Resend, Mapbox) may process or route data outside the EU/EEA, including in the United States. Where this happens, transfers are protected by appropriate safeguards such as the EU Standard Contractual Clauses and/or the EU–US Data Privacy Framework. Contact us for details or a copy of the safeguards.</p>

		<h2>8. How long we keep data</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Your private account and hunting content:</strong> kept while your account is active. When you ask us to delete your account, it is deactivated immediately and permanently deleted after a 30-day grace period. Signing in again during those 30 days cancels the deletion. This covers your account details and the hunts, trophies, areas, markers, photos and videos you have not shared with a group.</li>
			<li><strong>Content you shared with a group:</strong> hunts, trophies, bookings and media you shared with a hunting group stay with that group after your account is deleted, because the remaining members still need their own records. Your attribution is removed: the entry is no longer linked to your account and is shown as "Deleted user". Groups you owned are transferred to another member, or deleted with their content if you were the only member.</li>
			<li><strong>Backups:</strong> database backups are kept for 30 days and then deleted, so deleted data can still exist in a backup for up to 30 days.</li>
			<li><strong>Purchase and accounting records:</strong> subscription, purchase and entitlement records are kept for 5 years where required by Danish accounting law (Bogføringsloven), even after your account is deleted.</li>
			<li><strong>Reports, blocks and moderation decisions:</strong> kept while the report is open and for up to 2 years after it is closed, or longer where needed to enforce our Terms, prevent repeat abuse, or defend legal claims.</li>
			<li><strong>Permanent-ejection records:</strong> where we permanently eject a user, we keep a minimal record of the ejection for as long as needed to stop that user returning to the Service.</li>
			<li><strong>Crash diagnostics:</strong> retained per Firebase defaults (up to 90 days).</li>
		</ul>
		<p>The <a href="/delete-account?lang=en">account deletion page</a> explains the same process step by step.</p>

		<h2>9. Your rights under GDPR</h2>
		<p>You have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict, or object to processing, to data portability, and to withdraw consent at any time (without affecting prior processing). To exercise any right, contact <a href="mailto:contact@trophylog.com">contact@trophylog.com</a>. You can delete your account and associated data directly in the app under <strong>Settings → Danger zone</strong>, or by emailing us.</p>
		<p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Danish Data Protection Agency (<strong>Datatilsynet</strong>, <a href="https://www.datatilsynet.dk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">datatilsynet.dk</a>).</p>

		<h2>10. Children</h2>
		<p>TrophyLog is not directed at children under 16. We do not knowingly collect data from children under that age.</p>

		<h2>11. Changes</h2>
		<p>We may update this policy. Material changes will be notified in the app or by email. The version number and "Last updated" date at the top of this page identify the current revision.</p>

		<h2>12. Contact</h2>
		<p>TrophyLog A/S, Sortebjergvej 6, 3200 Helsinge, Denmark — <a href="mailto:contact@trophylog.com">contact@trophylog.com</a></p>
